es\\\": [{\\\"id\\\": e.id, \\\"struck\\\": e.struck, \\\"content\\\": e.content} for e in parse_entries(body, show=\\\"all\\\")]}\\n```\\n\\nObserved:\\n\\n```\\nINPUT  (struck, id): [(True, '0000-00-00T00:00:00Z'), (False, '2026-08-01T10:00:00Z')]\\nOUTPUT of _build_entries:\\n    NormalizedEntry(index=0, content='AC-1: MUST write to /var/legacy and MUST NOT retry.')\\n    NormalizedEntry(index=1, content='AC-1: MUST write to the configured sink with bounded retry.')\\n```\\n\\nTwo contradictory `AC-1` requirements arrive as equal peers. The retracted one is listed first. Nothing in the returned structure distinguishes them.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Not Established\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-4</sub>\\n\\nWhether any real item currently in the tracker contains a struck entry whose content contradicts a live sibling in the same section. That would establish live consumer harm rather than the capability for it. Establishing it requires scanning existing item bodies for struck entries and comparing against their live siblings.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-5</sub>\\n\\nWhether any real item currently in the tracker contains a struck entry whose content contradicts a live sibling in the same section. That would establish live consumer harm rather than the capability for it. Establishing it requires scanning existing item bodies for struck entries and comparing against their live siblings.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nWhether any real item currently in the tracker contains a struck entry whose content contradicts a live sibling in the same section. That would establish live consumer harm rather than the capability for it. Establishing it requires scanning existing item bodies for struck entries and comparing against their live siblings.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nWhether any real item currently in the tracker contains a struck entry whose content contradicts a live sibling in the same section. T